ext-align:center;color:#64696d;margin:0 auto 27px;max-width:720px;line-height:1.55}.bbr-pgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}.bbr-p{background:#fff;border-radius:12px;padding:26px;border:1px solid #d9d2c4}.bbr-p em{display:block;color:#a17e38;font:900 10px Arial;letter-spacing:.12em;font-style:normal}.bbr-p h3{font:26px/1.12 Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0}.bbr-p p{color:#595f64;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}.bbr-flow{margin-top:18px;font-size:11px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.04em}.bbr-why{max-width:1220px;margin:auto;padding:64px 22px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr;gap:44px;align-items:center}.bbr-why h2{font:clamp(36px,4vw,52px)/1.05 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 12px}.bbr-why>div>p{color:#60666a;line-height:1.65}.bbr-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}.bbr-li{background:#fff;border:1px solid #ded8cb;border-radius:10px;padding:17px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4}.bbr-li b{color:#a7833c;margin-right:7px}.bbr-ref{background:#fff;border-top:1px solid #ddd8cc}.bbr-refin{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:55px 22px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:30px;align-items:center}.bbr-ref h2{font:36px/1.08 Georgia,serif;margin:7px 0 10px}.bbr-ref p{max-width:700px;color:#5d6267;line-height:1.6;margin:0}.bbr-ref small{display:block;margin-top:10px;color:#7a7e81;line-height:1.45}.bbr-refbtns{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px;min-width:240px}.bbr-ref button,.bbr-ref a{min-height:44px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #a88743;background:#17191c;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:10px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.06em;padding:0 15px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;cursor:pointer}.bbr-ref a{background:#f7f5ef;color:#17191c}.bbr-final{background:#101010;color:#fff}.bbr-fin{max-width:1220px;margin:auto;padding:55px 22px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:25px}.bbr-fin h2{font:38px/1.04 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 9px}.bbr-fin p{margin:0;color:#cdd1d4}.bbr-fin .bbr-actions{margin:0}@media(max-width:900px){.bbr-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr}.bbr-photo{min-height:150px;order:2}.bbr-copy{padding:40px 28px 44px}.bbr-metrics{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.bbr-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.bbr-pgrid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.bbr-why{grid-template-columns:1fr}.bbr-refin{grid-template-columns:1fr}.bbr-refbtns{min-width:0;flex-direction:row}}@media(max-width:620px){.bbr-photo{display:block}.bbr-copy h1{font-size:40px}.bbr-metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.bbr-metric{padding:14px 8px}.bbr-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px}.bbr-sec,.bbr-prog,.bbr-why{padding:44px 24px}.bbr-head{display:block}.bbr-head h2,.bbr-prog h2,.bbr-why h2,.bbr-ref h2{font-size:31px}.bbr-p h3{font-size:23px}.bbr-head p{margin-top:12px}.bbr-list{display:block}.bbr-li{background:transparent;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #ded8cb;border-radius:0;padding:15px 4px}.bbr-li:last-child{border-bottom:0}.bbr-refin{padding:42px 24px}.bbr-refbtns{flex-direction:column}.bbr-fin{padding:42px 24px 56px;display:block}.bbr-fin .bbr-actions{margin-top:20px;display:grid}}</style><section class=\"bbr-hero\"><div class=\"bbr-copy\"><div class=\"bbr-ey\">REAL REVIEWS. SPECIFIC WORK.</div><h1>Strong Students Don’t Need More Noise.</h1><div class=\"bbr-lead\">They need to know what is actually breaking down.</div><p>My job is to find the failure point and build a useful fix. On the SAT that may be evidence, pacing, classification, or a repeated error. With EF it may be planning, initiation, organization, or follow-through.</p><div class=\"bbr-actions\"><a class=\"bbr-btn\" href=\"/book-consultation\">BOOK A CONSULTATION →</a><a class=\"bbr-btn alt\" href=\"https://www.wyzant.com/Tutors/MA/Brookline/10206436/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">VIEW VERIFIED REVIEWS →</a></div></div><div class=\"bbr-photo\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Behavioral Bridge student looking toward a mountain horizon\"></div></section><div class=\"bbr-metrics\"><div class=\"bbr-metric\"><b>5.0</b><span>Wyzant rating</span></div><div class=\"bbr-metric\"><b>75+</b><span>5-star reviews</span></div><div class=\"bbr-metric\"><b>350+</b><span>Wyzant + Superprof hours</span></div><div class=\"bbr-metric\"><b>Nearly 14</b><span>Years experience</span></div><div class=\"bbr-metric\"><b>SAT + EF</b><span>Two core services</span></div><div class=\"bbr-metric\"><b>Online</b><span>Remote nationwide</span></div></div><section class=\"bbr-sec\"><div class=\"bbr-head\"><div><small>PUBLIC REVIEWS & RECOMMENDATIONS</small><h2>What Families Actually Mention</h2></div><p>Across public feedback, themes recur: preparation, structure, patience, targeted diagnosis, and student rapport.</p></div><div class=\"bbr-grid\">${cards}</div><div class=\"bbr-reviewfoot\"><a href=\"https://www.wyzant.com/Tutors/MA/Brookline/10206436/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">VIEW ALL WYZANT REVIEWS →</a><a href=\"https://www.superprof.com/elite-english-reading-and-writing-tutor-improving-literacy-essays-and-academic-skills-perfect-wyzant-star-reviews-275.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SUPERPROF RECOMMENDATION →</a><span class=\"bbr-note\">Cards paraphrase public Wyzant reviews and one Superprof recommendation. Individual results vary; no score change is guaranteed.</span></div></section><section class=\"bbr-progress\"><div class=\"bbr-prog\"><h2>What I Actually Measure</h2><p>A score matters. So does the process behind it. I want to know whether the student can make the better decision again when the context changes.</p><div class=\"bbr-pgrid\"><article class=\"bbr-p\"><em>SAT PERFORMANCE</em><h3>Find the leak before adding volume</h3><p>Figure out whether the problem is content, classification, evidence, execution, pacing, or review. Then practice that failure point instead of random questions.</p><div class=\"bbr-flow\">CLASSIFY → ACTIVATE → PREDICT → PROVE</div></article><article class=\"bbr-p\"><em>EXECUTIVE FUNCTION</em><h3>Make the invisible process visible</h3><p>Planning, starting, sustaining, recovering, and finishing are different skills. Build around the broken link, then reduce support as the student owns it.</p><div class=\"bbr-flow\">CAPTURE → PLAN → PRIORITIZE → START → FINISH</div></article><article class=\"bbr-p\"><em>ACADEMIC SUPPORT</em><h3>Support should become less necessary</h3><p>The goal is not a student who needs a tutor forever. It is a student who can run the process with less prompting and more independence.</p><div class=\"bbr-flow\">ATTEMPT → DIAGNOSE → FIX → REDO → TRANSFER</div></article></div></div></section><section class=\"bbr-why\"><div><div class=\"bbr-ey\">HOW I WORK</div><h2>Diagnose first. Then build the system.</h2><p>I do not hand every student the same plan. I watch how the student works, identify the failure point, teach a specific route, and see whether it transfers.</p></div><div class=\"bbr-list\"><div class=\"bbr-li\"><b>✓</b>Diagnosis before prescription</div><div class=\"bbr-li\"><b>✓</b>Accuracy before speed when timing is the issue</div><div class=\"bbr-li\"><b>✓</b>Practice tied to observed errors</div><div class=\"bbr-li\"><b>✓</b>Clear fix rules—not vague “be careful” advice</div><div class=\"bbr-li\"><b>✓</b>Parent communication that says what is actually happening</div><div class=\"bbr-li\"><b>✓</b>Independence is the endpoint</div></div></section><section class=\"bbr-ref\"><div class=\"bbr-refin\"><div><div class=\"bbr-ey\">FOR CURRENT FAMILIES</div><h2>If the Work Has Helped, Introductions Are Always Appreciated.</h2><p>Know a family who may need SAT or executive-function support? Feel free to introduce us. I’m happy to see whether Behavioral Bridge is a good fit.</p><div class=\"bbr-flow\">INTRODUCE A FAMILY → PAID FIRST SESSION → ONE COMPLIMENTARY SESSION</div><small>Referral thank-you is separate from reviews; no review is required.</small></div><div class=\"bbr-refbtns\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"bbr-share\">SHARE BEHAVIORAL BRIDGE</button><a href=\"mailto:Ryan_Carvalho@BehavioralBridge.org?subject=Behavioral%20Bridge%20Referral&body=My%20name:%0AFamily/student:%0AContact:%0ANotes:\">MAKE A DIRECT INTRODUCTION</a></div></div></section><section class=\"bbr-final\"><div class=\"bbr-fin\"><div><h2>Want to Know Whether I Think I Can Help?</h2><p>Send me the situation, timeline, and what you have already tried. I’ll tell you what I would start with rather than force the same plan on everyone.</p></div><div class=\"bbr-actions\"><a class=\"bbr-btn\" href=\"/book-consultation\">BOOK A CONSULTATION →</a><a class=\"bbr-btn alt\" href=\"mailto:Ryan_Carvalho@BehavioralBridge.org\">EMAIL ME DIRECTLY</a></div></div></section>`;var b=s.querySelector('#bbr-share');if(b)b.addEventListener('click',sh);m.insertBefore(s,m.firstChild)}hideNative(m,s)}function run(){setTimeout(render,70)}document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',run);run();new MutationObserver(run).observe(document.documentElement,{childList:true,subtree:true});window.addEventListener('popstate',run);document.addEventListener('click',function(){setTimeout(run,120)},true)})();</script>"
